    {
      "id": "claim_7d073e0a14154d49822dac2258cee836",
      "statement": "PetView's drag uses pointer capture on the element that owns the handlers (.body) so pointermove/up are not retargeted, clamps the sprite to the viewport minus the scaled box (72 * size.scale), and uses a 4px drag threshold so a pointerup that never moved toggles the control panel and speaks an idle line. Drag position is local (not persisted); only the selected skin and size persist to localStorage (dsh-pet-skin, dsh-pet-size) with clamped reads for missing/out-of-range indices.",
