      "id": "claim_a3a478f20da6415f88959478dbaa5d9c",
      "statement": "The Task Manager is a two-piece surface bridged by taskPanelStore: TaskManagerTrigger (conversation.session.header.actions, order 20) only calls taskPanelStore.openPanel on click, and TaskManagerView (shell.overlay, order 100) is root-scope, returns null when the store reports closed, and renders a full-screen overlay that closes on outside click. The list tab reads projectionValues.todos (a locally-declared TodoItem type mirroring dsh-session to avoid adding the dsh-tool-todo dependency). The flow tab builds a parentId lineage tree and lazily fetches a per-session LifecycleSnapshot via the injected lifecycle wrapper (unwrap of remote.skillForge.lifecycle), caching results and tracking loading/error per node.",
